# Pull command after every push

Whenever you successfully `git push` to `origin/main` (or tell the user a commit is pushed), **always end with a ready-to-paste TEST deploy command** for cPanel / sg-s2. Do not wait for the user to ask "Pull?".

## Default: TEST only

Never include production unless the user explicitly asked to deploy live / main site.

## Choose full vs quick

- **Full deploy** — new migrations, composer.lock / PHP deps, or other backend install steps:
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/test.bakeandgrill.mv && git pull origin main && cd backend && composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader && php artisan migrate --force && php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan view:clear && php artisan queue:restart && git log -1 --oneline
```

- **Quick pull** — admin UI / Blade / small PHP-only fixes with no new migrations:
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/test.bakeandgrill.mv && git pull origin main && cd backend && php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan view:clear && php artisan queue:restart && git log -1 --oneline
```

## Format

After the push summary, add a short line like:

> **TEST pull** (full/quick — one reason):

then the fenced command block. Mention the expected tip commit hash when known.

If TEST auto-deploy is configured (`docs/TEST_AUTO_DEPLOY.md`), note that test should pull immediately after CI is green via webhook (cron fallback ~1 min) — still include the manual command as a fallback.
